129	/// End-to-end coverage for spec-7-1's export flow, driven through the real
130	/// production object graph `sl` resolves for the download icon
131	/// (`MeusRegistrosScreen._onExportTap`'s exact `sl<ExportJobCubit>()`
132	/// call) — wired to the real `ExportRepositoryImpl` ->
133	/// `ExportRemoteDataSource` -> `ApiClient` -> `Dio` (both real
134	/// interceptors attached) -> this faked transport boundary only. No
135	/// device/simulator/CI exists yet (AGENTS.md).
136	///
137	/// Complements rather than duplicates this story's existing coverage:
138	/// `export_job_cubit_test.dart` already proves every I/O-matrix transition
139	/// against a hand-written fake `ExportRepository` (no real `Failure.
140	/// fromCode`/DTO decoding involved), `export_remote_data_source_test.dart`
141	/// proves the DTO mapping against a *mocked* `ApiClient`, and
142	/// `meus_registros_screen_test.dart`'s "export entry point" group proves
143	/// the tap -> picker -> `start()` -> sheet wiring against a fake
144	/// repository too. None of them drives a real `export-summary-create`/
145	/// `export-status-get` round trip — real URL building, real headers, the
146	/// real `RetryInterceptor.neverRetriedFunctions` exclusion, the real
147	/// `ExportJobStatusDto.toState()` + `Failure.fromCode` mapping off a real
148	/// decoded JSON payload — through the real `Timer.periodic` poll loop in
149	/// one job lifecycle.
150	///
151	/// Driven directly against `ExportJobCubit`'s own public API (`start()`),
152	/// not through `tester.tap`/`pumpAndSettle`: `start()` awaits genuine
153	/// async I/O (a real Dio round trip) and then a real 2s `Timer.periodic`
154	/// poll loop, and `pumpAndSettle` isn't guaranteed to wait for either —
155	/// same rationale `capture_flow_e2e_test.dart`/`chat_flow_e2e_test.dart`
156	/// already document for their own cubits. `_waitForState` lets each real
157	/// poll tick elapse in real wall-clock time rather than mixing in
158	/// `fake_async` (the project's own `network_pipeline_integration_test.dart`
159	/// already accepts real wall-clock delays the same way for
