Implemented spec-7-3-empty-period-handling.md exactly as scoped.

**Change (the only functional edit, per the spec's Boundaries):**
`lib/features/export/presentation/cubit/export_job_cubit.dart`, `start()`'s create-failure branch (previously lines 76-80, now ~76-90). Added an `is ExportEmptyPeriod` check before the generic failure handling:

```dart
return result.match(
  (failure) {
    if (failure is ExportEmptyPeriod) {
      emit(const ExportJobState.emptyPeriod());
      return true;
    }
    emit(ExportJobState.error(failure));
    return false;
  },
  (jobId) { ... },
);
```

This reuses the existing `Failure.exportEmptyPeriod`/`ExportEmptyPeriod` (AD-3) and the existing `ExportJobState.emptyPeriod()` — no new `Failure` subtype, no new `ExportJobState` variant, no string check on `failure.message`. `_jobId` stays `null` on this branch and `_startPolling()` is never called, so `MeusRegistrosScreen._onExportTap`'s `if (started) { ExportStatusSheet.show(...) }` opens the sheet directly on "Período vazio" with no underlying job. Every other create-failure subtype is untouched — still `ExportJobState.error(failure)` / returns `false`.

No other production file was touched (`ExportJobState`, `ExportJobStatusDto`, `ExportStatusSheet`, `MeusRegistrosScreen` all left as read-only per the spec).

**Tests added (siblings to the spec's named anchors):**
1. `test/features/export/presentation/cubit/export_job_cubit_test.dart` — new test in the `start — Create job` group, right after the existing "Create fails" test: queues `createJobResult = left(Failure.exportEmptyPeriod(...))`, asserts `started` is `true`, `cubit.state is ExportJobEmptyPeriod`, and that elapsing a poll interval never calls `getStatus` (fake repository, `fakeAsync`).
2. `test/features/export/export_flow_e2e_test.dart` — new test right after the existing poll-path "Período vazio" e2e test: queues a single real `400 {code: EXPORT_EMPTY_PERIOD, message, retryable: false}` response to `export-summary-create` via the faked `HttpClientAdapter`, drives the real DI-resolved `ExportJobCubit` through the real `ExportRepositoryImpl`/`Failure.fromCode` pipeline, asserts `started` is `true`, `cubit.state is ExportJobEmptyPeriod`, exactly one request ever left, and no `export-status-get` request appears even after a 3s real-time wait.

Also checked off the three Tasks & Acceptance checkboxes in `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-7-3-empty-period-handling.md` (outside the frozen Intent/Boundaries block, so editable).

**Verification run:**
- `fvm flutter analyze` → "No issues found!"
- `fvm flutter test test/features/export/` → all 67 tests pass, including both new ones.
- `fvm flutter test` (full suite) → all 1130 tests pass — confirmed the `Failure`-hierarchy touch didn't regress anything elsewhere.

**Incomplete/risky:** nothing left incomplete against the spec's scope. One minor judgment call: I also updated the three `- [ ]` checkboxes to `- [x]` in the spec file's Tasks & Acceptance section (not inside the frozen block) to reflect completion — easy to revert if you'd rather leave that file untouched.

